From: Leo <62428370+LeoooChen@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iwinfo: return an error when txpower is unknown

Signal failure instead of reporting 0 dBm when nl80211 has no txpower
information, so LuCI can show an unknown state rather than a wrong
value.

Signed-off-by: Leo <62428370+LeoooChen@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/iwinfo_nl80211.c
+++ b/iwinfo_nl80211.c
@@ -1650,10 +1650,10 @@
 	char *res;
 
 	res = nl80211_phy2ifname(ifname);
-	*buf = 0;
+	*buf = INT_MIN;
 
 	if (nl80211_request(res ? res : ifname, NL80211_CMD_GET_INTERFACE, 0,
-	                    nl80211_get_txpower_cb, buf))
+	                    nl80211_get_txpower_cb, buf) || *buf == INT_MIN)
 		return -1;
 
 	return 0;
